title: Fileless Execution via memfd_create
id: 41af8b0f-e11a-4844-bc95-5979ddf0c1a6
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of a process backed by an anonymous in-memory file (an executable path under /proc/self/fd or an anonymous memfd region), the memfd_create reflective-loading technique that runs binaries without touching disk.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1620/
logsource:
  product: linux
  category: process_creation
detection:
  selection:
    Image|contains:
      - '/memfd:'
      - 'memfd:'
    CommandLine|contains: 'memfd'
  condition: selection
fields:
  - CommandLine
  - User
  - Image
falsepositives:
  - Rare legitimate use of anonymous files
level: high
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1620
